Root cause identified: `RequestGuard::user()` caches the user and `setRequest()` never resets it, so sequential requests in the same test reuse a stale cached user despite token revocation. This is a test lifecycle artifact (each real HTTP request gets a fresh guard). I'll split the test into separate methods, each resolving guards freshly — the canonical way to test token revocation.
